---
import FlowShot from '../FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import shotDomains from '../../../assets/flow/shots/settings-models.webp';
import detailDomains from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-domains.webp';
---
<section class="border-t border-border/60 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-domains">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Trust boundaries</p>
    <h3 id="tour-domains" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">Set the boundary before the model.</h3>
    <p class="of-lede mt-5" data-animate="rise">Local, LAN, Cloud prepaid, and Cloud postpaid each have their own switch and plain statement of locality and cost. Flow may discover a working provider, but discovery never enables it. A fallback that would cross a boundary stops and asks.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">Cost is compared before the run and observed after it. Local work records no charge because none was owed.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="of-stage of-stage--pad-bottom mt-12" data-animate="plate">
    <FlowShot src={shotDomains} alt="Flow's Models settings: provider keys held in Flow Keychain and the Local execution domain switched on with Ollama, LM Studio and Flow Runtime, beside a document that records why local models were chosen." sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 78rem, (min-width: 1024px) 64rem, 100vw" />
    <FlowDetail class="of-stage__detail of-stage__detail--bl" src={detailDomains} alt="Flow's Local domain enabled, stating that work stays on this Mac and showing three discovered providers offered to Smart Routing." caption="One switch per domain · Discovery never enables" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 30rem, (min-width: 1024px) 27rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" animate />
  </div>
</section>
